    1226: d = await fetchJSON(_evUrl(ctx, what, params));   // catch -> error into p
    1231: if (!p.isConnected) return;         // view changed while loading
    1232: if (d.error) { p.innerHTML = …; return; }
    1233: p.innerHTML = render(d);
    1234: p.scrollIntoView({ block: "nearest", behavior: "smooth" });
    ```
  - Close (1357-1361): delegated, `const close = t.closest("[data-ev-close]"); if (close) { const p = _evPanel(); if (p) p.innerHTML = ""; return; }` — the `close` button is `<button class="ev-close" type="button" data-ev-close="1">close</button>` inside `_evCtxLine` (1248). **Closing = emptying innerHTML; visibility is entirely CSS**: styles.css:742 ` .arch-evidence:empty { display: none; }`.
  - `_wireEvidence(box)` (1354-1420) is a **delegated** click listener on the results box, guarded once by `box.dataset.evWired = "1"` (1355-1356), because the panel innerHTML is replaced wholesale. Handler order inside (1357-1418): `[data-ev-close]` → `[data-lemma-toggle]` → bail if `!_ARCH_CTX` (1377) → `[data-arch-rule]` → `[data-arch-word]` → `[data-ev-par]` → `[data-ev-ngram]` → `[data-ev-loci]`.
  - Position/layout: **not a modal, not a sidebar, not fixed** — it is an inline block rendered at the bottom of the report's own results area, immediately after `.arch-table`, styled as a bordered card (styles.css:743-747) and scrolled into view with `block: "nearest"`. Renderers: `_evCtxLine` (1237-1249), `_evHits` (1251-1261), `_evLociHtml` (1263-1289), `_evNgramsHtml` (1291-1321), `_evParallelHtml` (1323-1348). Panel classes used: `ev-head`, `ev-close`, `ev-cols`, `ev-cap`, `ev-kwic`, `ev-parallel`, `ev-locus`, `ev-context`, `ev-marked` (class on `<mark>`), `ev-mini`, `ev-score`, `ev-shared`, `ev-note`, `ev-actions`.

  For a dictionary panel on the reader you would mirror this exactly: a `<div id="dict-evidence" class="arch-evidence">` (or new `dict-panel` reusing the same CSS) inside `.reader-pane`, plus a delegated click listener bound on `#text` / the pane after `loadSection` writes innerHTML (note: `#text.innerHTML` is replaced on every section load, so the listener must be attached to a stable ancestor — the `#text` div itself survives, or use the `.reader-pane`/`$view()`).

  ## 5. `exportCmpResults()` — app.js:777-838

  ```js
  777: function exportCmpResults() {
  778:   if (!_cmpLast || !_cmpLast.result || !_cmpLast.result.pairs.length) { toast("No results to export yet."); return; }
  ...  head = [ ...29 TSV column names... ]            // 781-791
  810: ].map((x) => (x == null ? "" : String(x)).replace(/\t/g, " ")).join("\t");
  811: const lines = [head.join("\t")];            // rows sorted by chain_len desc, 814-816
  817: const cs = r.cluster_stats || {};
  818-827: const blob = new Blob(["# KONI Flame — Result list (TSV)\n", "# n-gram=…  mode=…  threshold=…\n#\n", lines.join("\n")],
  828:                            { type: "text/tab-separated-values;charset=utf-8" });
  829: const a = document.createElement("a");
  830: a.href = URL.createObjectURL(blob);
  831-833: a.download = `koni_flame_${f1}.${g1}_vs_${f2}.${g2}.tsv`;
  834: document.body.appendChild(a); a.click();
  835: setTimeout(() => { URL.revokeObjectURL(a.href); a.remove(); }, 1000);
  836: toast(`${r.pairs.length} rows exported (TSV).`);
  ```
  Style to match: **Blob + `URL.createObjectURL`** (no data URI), MIME `text/tab-separated-values;charset=utf-8`, a `#`-prefixed metadata header block before the column header, tabs stripped from values, filename pattern `koni_flame_{aid}.{wid}_vs_{aid}.{wid}.tsv`, immediate revoke via `setTimeout(…, 1000)`, and a `toast()` confirmation. Trigger: button created at app.js:560 `<button id="cmp-export" class="more-btn" title="Download the current result list (TSV)">⤓ Export results</button>`, listener bound at app.js:567 `document.getElementById("cmp-export").addEventListener("click", exportCmpResults);`. Result state lives in `_cmpLast` (declared 409, filled 429/476-518).

  ## 6. localStorage and keyboard

  - **Only one key: `"opentgl"`**, accessed solely through the `settings` object (app.js:20-26):
    ```js
    22: try { return JSON.parse(localStorage.getItem("opentgl") || "{}"); } catch { return {}; }
    25: save(o) { localStorage.setItem("opentgl", JSON.stringify(o)); },
    ```
    Shape is a flat object `{ size?: number, lh?: number, theme?: "light"|"dark" }` (defaults `20 / 1.8 / "light"`, app.js:29). Writers: `changeSize` (37), `cycleLineHeight` (45), `toggleTheme` (52); reader applies via `applySettings()` (27-33) setting CSS vars `--reader-size`, `--reader-lh` on `document.documentElement` and `document.body.dataset.theme`. No other localStorage/sessionStorage/indexedDB use in the app (a stale `app.js.bak.20260629-123422` also contains the same two lines — ignore).
  - **No keyboard shortcut handling at all**: no `keydown`/`keyup`/`keypress`/`e.key`/`tabindex`/`onsubmit` anywhere in app.js or index.html. UI events are `hashchange` (app.js:1741) plus per-element `click`/`input`/`change` listeners, and the four masthead icon buttons wired at app.js:1742-1745 (`font-inc`, `font-dec`, `lh-toggle`, `theme-toggle`). Also no `window.getSelection` / `selectionchange` usage — word-selection annotations would be greenfield.

  ## 7. CSS map — styles.css

  Section boundaries (comment headers): masthead 74; layout shell 116; home/search 130; author page 183; **reader 253**; sources panel 318; toast 394; compare 404; pickers 565; streaming progress 604; archaism 633; three-corpus badges 706; evidence panel 741; responsive 829; very-narrow 850.

  - **Reader layout (253-316)** — add new reader styles here:
    - `.reader` 254 `display:grid; grid-template-columns: 13rem 1fr; gap:2.6rem; align-items:start;`
    - `.reader-nav` 255-259 (sticky sidebar: `position:sticky; top:4.6rem; max-height:calc(100vh - 6rem); overflow:auto; border-right`), `.reader-nav h4` 260
    - `.nav-item` 266-272 (block button: `border:none; background:none; width:100%; text-align:left; cursor:pointer`), `.nav-item:hover` 273, `.nav-item.active` 274 (`color:var(--accent)`), `.nav-item .nav-meta` 275
    - `.reader-pane` 277, `.reader-title` 278-281, `.reader-title .gr` 282, `.reader-sub` 283-286, `.reader-sub .urn` 287, `.reader-sub .w-edition` 288, `.w-edition` 289-292
    - `.greek-text` 294-300 (`font-family: var(--font-greek); font-size: var(--reader-size); line-height: var(--reader-lh); max-width: 44rem`), `.greek-text .block-head` 301-306, `.greek-text .para` 307, `.greek-text .line` 308-310 (grid `3rem 1fr`), `.greek-text .line .lnum` 311-315, `.greek-text .line .ltext` 316 (`white-space: pre-wrap`)
  - **Sources panel (318-364)**: `.sources`, `.sources > summary` (+`::before` ▸/▾), `.src-list` (max-height collapse animation), `.src-link` (+`.confirmed`, `.search`), `.src-badge`, `.src-body`, `.src-label`, `.src-detail`, `.src-kind`.
  - **Panel/status helpers**: `.reader-empty` 366-369, `.spinner` 370-374, `.stats` 375-382, `.more-btn` 384-391 (the universal secondary button: hairline border, `border-radius: var(--radius)`, small-caps sans — used by `#cmp-export`, `#arch-go`, `#more-btn`, `ev` action buttons), `#count` 392. `.toast` 395-402.
  - **Evidence panel (741-827)**: `.arch-evidence:empty { display:none }` 742, `.arch-evidence` 743-747 (card: `border:1px solid var(--rule); border-radius:var(--radius); background:var(--bg-elev)`), hover-affordance rules `.arch-table td[data-arch-word]`/`[data-arch-rule]` 750-753, `.arch-table tr[data-lemma-toggle]` 757-758, `tr.lemma-forms` 759-761, `.ev-head` 762-767, `.ev-close` 768-774, `.ev-cap` 775-778, `.ev-cols` 779, `.ev-kwic, .ev-parallel` 780-785, `.ev-locus` 786-789, `.ev-context` 790, `.ev-context mark, .ev-parallel mark` 793-796, `.ev-mini` 797-802, `.ev-score` 803-806, `.ev-shared` 807-811, `.ev-note` 812-813, `.ev-actions` 814-817, `.ev-actions input[type=number]` 818-823, narrow-screen overrides 824-827.
  - **Badges/pills**: `.author-meta .pill` 195, `.work .badge` 235, `.src-badge` 351, `.cmp-score` 457-463 (outlined `--match`), `.cmp-cluster-count` 484-489 (outlined `--accent`), `.arch-class` 711-716 + variants 717-721 (`arch-class-archaism|classical|overused|avoided|shared`), `.arch-tag` 730-736. Buttons: `.icon-btn` 105, `.more-btn` 384, `.flame-btn` 594-602, `.ev-close` 768, `.ev-mini` 797, `.nav-item` 266.
  - Design tokens (styles.css:5-49): `--font-greek`/`--font-ui`/`--font-meta`, `--reader-size`, `--reader-lh`, `--radius:2px`, `--bg`, `--bg-elev`, `--bg-soft`, `--text`, `--text-soft`, `--text-faint`, `--rule`, `--rule-strong`, `--accent`, `--accent-soft`, `--match`, `--match-bg`, `--bridge`, `--bridge-bg`; dark overrides under `body[data-theme="dark"]`.
  - Responsive: 830-846 collapses `.reader` to one column and un-sticks `.reader-nav` at ≤760px; if you add a right-hand dictionary column, add its collapse here too.

  ## Gotchas worth knowing before writing code
  - `renderReader` and `runArchaism` both wipe `$view().innerHTML`, and `loadSection` wipes `#text.innerHTML` — any listener must be delegated on a surviving ancestor (`#text` itself survives section switches; `.reader-pane`/`$view()` survive everything).
  - `readerState` is currently dead state; nothing resets it when leaving the reader.
  - The reader payload has no word offsets/lemmas: `b.text` is one escaped string per block, and the section endpoints are `/api/text/{aid}/{wid}/section/{idx}` (blocks) and `/api/text/{aid}/{wid}/sections` (TOC). Any per-word dictionary lookup or annotation anchoring needs either client-side tokenization (matching the existing `esc()` output, which would break the current `textContent`-only render) or a new backend field.
  - Existing style conventions to match: small-caps `--font-meta` for apparatus, `var(--radius)` 2px corners, hairline `var(--rule)` borders, one accent, `toast()` for feedback, `esc()` for every interpolated string.

